db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8211c4cd-3987-50aa-bbab-1eb34628bdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460351} {:answer/id #uuid "290cf3d8-4b61-5cc4-9af1-edffda741505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8211c4cd-3987-50aa-bbab-1eb34628bdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460351} :answer-field/id #uuid "d06ed8cb-621c-5eb2-8e91-0dbdff9927a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b249c3f7-b17f-5e21-a581-a52a50cd8b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-87154" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n- **I.** The weight, in kilograms, of sugar in a randomly selected bag with a capacity of $1\\,\\text{kg}$\n- **II.** The number of students in a randomly selected classroom\n- **III.** The outcome of flipping a coin\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nSome common examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,1].$\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,3,…,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are heads or tails, which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049254 :topic/id #uuid "e6f9ad03-abe7-52d6-8a6a-acbcb8fbeef7" :topic/math-academy-id 1351 :topic/title "Singular Linear Transformations in the Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d70c49cc-47a0-5157-b9e8-1a55f6a9d0b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460473} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ebc32-6d79-5d58-bfb1-01412c4b840d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ebc32-6d79-5d58-bfb1-01412c4b840d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460474} :answer-field/id #uuid "c05c7404-e1f5-59ac-8224-db0b6e2cd44a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40bf32c8-3c87-58ba-9995-948cb586c6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460475} {:answer/id #uuid "d98120ae-3c78-5a9f-afe8-13a7d12e3df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d98120ae-3c78-5a9f-afe8-13a7d12e3df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460476} :answer-field/id #uuid "c298a4be-cad1-5acb-83fe-f64df13fe125" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e31242f-1ccc-567c-b85d-6f4e22f24d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460477} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8ba8f6-b11f-5b8e-8aa8-ac18d8c7e850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e31242f-1ccc-567c-b85d-6f4e22f24d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460477} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46b6209-20d1-54b6-9102-6a18630bf5a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd611935-717e-54db-b36b-c834b2cac00c" :question/math-academy-id "q-96858" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,1)$, $(2,1)$ and $(1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-2,1)$\n- **II.** $(-8,4)$\n- **III.** $(3,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-8,4)$, $(-12,6)$ and $(-2,1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049892 :topic/id #uuid "1c2006c0-c4c4-5ff8-8fa2-7f9dd3693f49" :topic/math-academy-id 1500 :topic/title "Collinear Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971706ed-5d46-504e-aa4d-2a21056bd264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477133} {:answer/id #uuid "bc542e30-ca0c-5e6f-8554-8e9575d63c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc542e30-ca0c-5e6f-8554-8e9575d63c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477134} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f67f467-b163-5587-bb4a-c67ee1ede00d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477536} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "262beea7-6449-51e5-9496-d6d71ceb7250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477135} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4190c2-3b72-5c8f-b865-b2f689744c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "262beea7-6449-51e5-9496-d6d71ceb7250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477135} :answer-field/id #uuid "30995247-2b75-510c-b0ff-dfd7d6a07d7f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5a9583e-fee0-5614-8ddd-0c4fdac14975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477137} {:answer/id #uuid "49cb4428-0d4a-5ea1-82cb-052da618d68b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49cb4428-0d4a-5ea1-82cb-052da618d68b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477138} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba267e9d-e2a0-5385-8f0c-ecd8fd2c153b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5df118a-6629-591e-bac9-243a7536e271" :question/math-academy-id "q-13445" :question/problem "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,N,R$\n\nII. $P,S,T$\n\nIII. $O,P,S$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $M,N,R$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/b8/b8fae613772422b14fce2e2db0762f659599f0b17409223ec291802b5d760d9c.png)\n\n- $P,S,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/85/85638c1466360f3e5285c34e84903824140b9e2fc72a0f029ab1ded170b64eb2.png)\n\n- $O,P,S$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/4b/4b7ef30e306e3c7e70dadb1524e1f60a9ea01832215009ef2ea8344cb07e7297.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049892 :topic/id #uuid "1c2006c0-c4c4-5ff8-8fa2-7f9dd3693f49" :topic/math-academy-id 1500 :topic/title "Collinear Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7afd290-acc0-55c6-998c-768cd7580391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477145} {:answer/id #uuid "6bfad2eb-0602-548b-9e77-506210b3bc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bfad2eb-0602-548b-9e77-506210b3bc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477146} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e823520-ee6e-57c6-8866-ce7228855732" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "230de8f6-d07e-5dba-8bcc-a3b9c8b2125d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477147} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5146f6-0447-5fc5-bd68-f40aecec77f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "230de8f6-d07e-5dba-8bcc-a3b9c8b2125d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477147} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3bcafbf-d3e7-5c54-9da4-95aaae9dbd92" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d20b0e0d-f3a1-50f1-9b8e-686d5326c162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477149} {:answer/id #uuid "c6bfc265-5ff0-51aa-b51f-40156f7ba1cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6bfc265-5ff0-51aa-b51f-40156f7ba1cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477150} :answer-field/id #uuid "d716b6f3-8e54-5ea0-9948-1e07367c1482" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ea9e0d7-7c8f-5224-8f6f-e5c31c36ab4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-155503" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb96a7692787ca6e055b41d4f1599b87baa1ea331544ea42235a7131343c76e3.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/54/54735541d4dfc424fe186ddabe0c3f9d3cbd45a0dc7a1b8f4551cf8c5e5bc14f.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/f0/f00f882c97fd201178e54f29151a48a4f41d4108cf375104cc338e968c55761b.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/6e/6e0c0320775d93364e32655d1e09081382078fa7e96fbe621a8c558f63dfcabb.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049310 :topic/id #uuid "eb6655db-68e9-5ef3-bf7a-81223e92dac0" :topic/math-academy-id 1414 :topic/title "Linear Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ec6698b-966d-5e31-b760-5faeba4367be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438040 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574008 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111133} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} {:answer/id #uuid "ce68107b-c73c-5910-8bb8-b2dd40c29da8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec6698b-966d-5e31-b760-5faeba4367be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/v