academy-id "q-29095" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n- **I.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=10$\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation II has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115181 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9a3d8db-a6e0-5c96-9c75-415d4a75cf4d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With No Solutions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049220 :topic/id #uuid "e46861d7-4b7a-5813-a6e8-914206606355" :topic/math-academy-id 1565 :topic/title "Elementary Trigonometric Equations Containing Secant"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d39680-0a9b-53ff-b5ab-4e090a52a0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477209} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1849d1-0c56-5404-9fea-93d23d5ce43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d39680-0a9b-53ff-b5ab-4e090a52a0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477209} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbe10ae-a6bf-532b-82df-343278c37366" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05db1bb3-08cf-5663-86bc-27656e52c7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477211} {:answer/id #uuid "8b44d26c-8476-594a-aaea-1cb1072d284e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05db1bb3-08cf-5663-86bc-27656e52c7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477211} :answer-field/id #uuid "9369458e-e7ef-5d9c-ba7b-821fc4670624" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69dde8dc-6640-50b4-8ec5-4ec7ea0e2f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477213} {:answer/id #uuid "76ce1019-8cd8-5e6c-b737-3373574e089e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76ce1019-8cd8-5e6c-b737-3373574e089e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477214} :answer-field/id #uuid "196aa8ab-5b05-5051-95e5-950aff40162e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fcb31a9b-9679-5d24-8bf7-7929bd2e8a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-29163" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nI. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=1$\nII. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=2$\nIII. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b255edc3-168a-53c5-b7fd-130015d89dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448528} {:answer/id #uuid "611f1bf3-f572-5071-af7b-5ccec271f643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b255edc3-168a-53c5-b7fd-130015d89dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448528} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1f6a11-7b45-59b9-903a-c0c2471fc798" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72baf1e1-9212-5021-a585-481f5bba74ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448530} {:answer/id #uuid "5e276ac6-bcc0-52ec-95fa-40286a8ed55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e276ac6-bcc0-52ec-95fa-40286a8ed55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448531} :answer-field/id #uuid "e99c7157-f302-5e53-8128-5ad21c42eced" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739696ce-d403-55e8-84ee-8d3e335d054a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448532} {:answer/id #uuid "69f959b7-8280-52e8-83d2-0668cd0d8df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739696ce-d403-55e8-84ee-8d3e335d054a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448532} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc4bffcd-c4c4-562e-ba66-83ea5b73f808" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44e70f28-a4b9-56ce-989d-752d9ef0f612" :question/math-academy-id "q-32088" :question/problem "Let \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$\n- **III.** ${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the first part of the invertible matrix theorem, the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ must exist.\n\nFinally, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176de855-4a3b-551d-9a6d-c5e1d00a567a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448534} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b98725-434c-5b83-8ee3-06d0970e94ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0b98725-434c-5b83-8ee3-06d0970e94ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448535} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbff0320-11a9-589e-bda3-7c6965059609" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554e90c0-e81b-5166-9625-296ed77b1cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448536} {:answer/id #uuid "059ccd63-55d7-5869-9f88-381300cafe9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "554e90c0-e81b-5166-9625-296ed77b1cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448536} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ab3b604-085e-5934-a7b5-08f1fefb3608" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2e883cb-4e77-5677-80d6-4bc9a7c57a12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448538} {:answer/id #uuid "8b90a5df-f67b-51b6-aff8-da963977b5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b90a5df-f67b-51b6-aff8-da963977b5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448539} :answer-field/id #uuid "a82022b1-d54d-538d-b7c1-7822cabdd846" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "947396a7-1dd0-5962-800b-c42f03f930a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32091" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+\\sqrt{7}y &=0.3 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{0.1}x+3y &=\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The lines $3x+\\sqrt{7}y=0.3$ and $-2\\sqrt{0.1}x+3y=\\sqrt{7}$ intersect exactly at one point\n\n- **II.** The determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $0$\n\n- **III.** The coefficient matrix is invertible" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n1\\. $A$ is invertible.\n\n2\\. The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n3\\. The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n4\\. The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n5\\. $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the determinant cannot be $0.$\n\n- Statement III is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b2036f-da0f-59de-8a39-6b33e6cbdd04" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a True Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a433b800-1989-563e-83e7-5397c5645766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459769} {:answer/id #uuid "f27cd420-457b-52b0-be46-420933044538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f27cd420-457b-52b0-be46-420933044538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459770} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cb2e9f1-fb8f-51c5-b00d-72cffd6f3c70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87a1cebe-01c8-5058-9714-b637af1f37da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459771} {:answer/id #uuid "b3681972-1d5a-565f-8458-5b8fb369970e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87a1cebe-01c8-5058-9714-b637af1f37da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459771} :answer-field/id #uuid "66227881-d1e0-51a9-ab58-2ae984608738" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aeb3e0e-1388-5c9a-acdc-1e8fd08c915c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459773} {:answer/id #uuid "b0269478-23f2-5548-a846-c1bfeff061d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0269478-23f2-5548-a846-c1bfeff061d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459774} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ad434b-4089-5c1e-9be7-18886b5005e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e42babae-3f60-5ad6-9c62-eaf91af5f106" :question/math-academy-id "q-32167" :question/problem "Which of the following completes the statement so that it is true:\n\n*If a $2\\times 2$-matrix $A$ is invertible, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ . *\n- **I.** $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution\n- **II.** $Ax=0$ has infinitely many solutions\n- **III.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\nNow, since the first part of the invertible matrix theorem is true ($A$ is invertible), all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only options I and III give us true statements:\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution.* $\\,✓$\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $det(A)\\ne 0.$* $\\,✓$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733 :topic/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4bdc967-dd67-5770-b3ba-57acb8064685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438106} {:answer/id #uuid "16d63261-26fa-564b-9a02-813ef69df1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4bdc967-dd67-5770-b3ba-57acb8064685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438106} :answer-field/id #uuid "48e752bf-5559-502a-9c5a-30d89ae8707e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd14eb1a-54cf-5d73-9b08-8904377c5fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438108} {:answer/id #uuid "05ef1b8f-126b-56bb-bda0-423f87e55922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ef1b8f-126b-56bb-bda0-423f87e55922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438109} :answer-field/id #uuid "343b74aa-4317-53b2-a41d-750a92184a1b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e68484e-ebe2-513a-9922-2e5462de62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438110} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe5eb6d-0b84-5bb3-929e-e95859bb6bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e68484e-ebe2-513a-9922-2e5462de62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438110} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d0bc1ed-439f-55dd-983f-394748aacbef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "402ab26a-a0df-5fc5-a264-b91a4c6d7d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-32242" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y &=6 \\\\ 2x-3y &=13 \\\\ 5x-y &=45\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system has a unique solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 75\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b39e27f-13ee-501b-ba4b-5d78eda71cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459859} {:answer/id #uuid "42bc3d2f-47ac-5240-bebc-29d8ead2b2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42bc3d2f-47ac-5240-bebc-29d8ead2b2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459860} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4b48c7-8b33-5b11-b0ff-fd23af78c621" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a88c44bd-6f41-5235-ac58-7911bde2559b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459861} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f3a730-a463-502e-ba29-0ea5209e14d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3f3a730-a463-502e-ba29-0ea5209e14d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459862} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e08014-03f2-546f-8c0e-728bfa9c9445" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6abd007-c716-5d06-8cfa-120ea1d604b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459863} {:answer/id #uuid "27573a68-3ee6-50f3-b43d-78e4538fb66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6abd007-c716-5d06-8cfa-120ea1d604b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459863} :answer-field/id #uuid "27edb236-0299-5bf2-b9d8-b04543e794ed" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f74e266c-1efa-53d7-993c-e40799d4cc74" :question/math-academy-id "q-36073" :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $A$ is invertible\n- **II.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $Ax=0$ has an infinite number of solutions\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733 :topic/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1eee681-520d-5d0a-802e-8d5b29c52974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438296} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ace7b5-89a9-5ece-ad6b-0ce43e80a049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2ace7b5-89a9-5ece-ad6b-0ce43e80a049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438297} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e35039-20ea-5f8c-9889-aaf209c08f8c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3d1f45-fc1a-5e10-a017-8a9199b3e295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438298} {:answer/id #uuid "039beb6d-4028-5582-9983-702125a74145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c3d1f45-fc1a-5e10-a017-8a9199b3e295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438298} :answer-field/id #uuid "168dcfad-47ff-5ee1-9214-61e870c730b0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae82757c-5e4b-593d-84dd-aca1302ca366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438300} {:answer/id #uuid "8f20a360-4b99-5b18-808c-9bab5fd09713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae82757c-5e4b-593d-84dd-aca1302ca366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438300} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b7ded78-a4d6-5805-8398-330746f91418" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e80c83a9-9107-528b-af57-73287d15e8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42061" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=0 \\\\ -4x+6y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733 :topic/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations"} :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425937} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425951}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048221 :topic/id #uuid "8959dd0b-8ef2-54bf-b8d9-d9b2606263cd" :topic/math-academy-id 1735 :topic/title "Partitioned and Block Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17aa9c3c-1177-5ab6-9436-4ed101b94dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459963} {:answer/id #uuid "37e030ed-add9-5c5c-b9c2-a9b03bda4a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17aa9c3c-1177-5ab6-9436-4ed101b94dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459963} :answer-field/id #uuid "575277b5-4a90-527e-97ae-d9ef4882fdfa" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3757cf46-44d8-5925-81e3-501b153e88c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459965} {:answer/id #uuid "9e164199-e408-5a69-9bc2-cd5d71bdf400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3757cf46-44d8-5925-81e3-501b153e88c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459965} :answer-field/id #uuid "053227d5-2248-514c-83ab-a486205fe2d4" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "921e04de-799e-5beb-ab08-d9814cdcfb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459967} {:answer/id #uuid "7574341a-6c1f-5a8e-961a-b129941c9412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7574341a-6c1f-5a8e-961a-b129941c9412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459968} :answer-field/id #uuid "9efeee9c-63b6-5691-bb36-c331fd5f912d" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12fdac9a-07ca-546f-8c67-8327e7b0318b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42134" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050122 :topic/id #uuid "2eaec2b9-4c03-5efd-b5aa-8e9655cca4f4" :topic/math-academy-id 1724 :topic/title "Properties of Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} {:answer/id #uuid "a3967aa3-4b50-5c5c-b5fe-aa477f5fe032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} :answer-field/id #uuid "149d811f-1bfd-59da-848a-31d1c4100def" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86075d40-0e3f-586b-9449-798158d86bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448634} {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cdc4938-08ac-5768-9c3a-6cf1b96bf157" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8546691d-f8b4-5754-96f8-903691eb5eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448636} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc3e7d1-fdc0-5ebf-9944-36f12a7d8eff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e648555-87e2-52bf-ac70-24ae7f7d32c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42265" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA$\n- **II.** $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n- **III.** $AC+BC=(A+B)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050122 :topic/id #uuid "2eaec2b9-4c03-5efd-b5aa-8e9655cca4f4" :topic/math-academy-id 1724 :topic/title "Properties of Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84adee91-f9b3-5089-890e-41b5e257813d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448638} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e31c4f-b7bd-5276-a991-deb172fd1702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e31c4f-b7bd-5276-a991-deb172fd1702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448639} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d1bd3d1-8fdb-5689-a908-f1bc0ac9ac01" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1670a685-9e94-5937-8cfd-7d0d29af6eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448640} {:answer/id #uuid "16ec1bf8-e36a-5bfb-84bd-a4334c07e464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1670a685-9e94-5937-8cfd-7d0d29af6eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448640} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b55508-2a98-5d52-9e53-d6536bd357ec" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113b4e99-4e5b-55aa-a4da-2a14a868af02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448642} {:answer/id #uuid "056450c3-2bbe-583e-950a-5fcae4730b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "113b4e99-4e5b-55aa-a4da-2a14a868af02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448642} :answer-field/id #uuid "96d5b3ee-a8ea-534b-8e66-6ca762d54d43" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "174631dd-f119-50e8-bf7b-ac669b330d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-42266" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(A+B)C=AC+BC$\n- **II.** $AB=BA$\n- **III.** $A(BC)=(BA)C$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC) &=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050576 :topic/id #uuid "54fffdff-21ee-5191-90e6-7d1d444eefd6" :topic/math-academy-id 1726 :topic/title "Elementary 2x2 Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a081c073-7785-5822-a590-7bfe5b3a0d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459993} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6c82a-ea16-5ff3-8bdf-84c0339a862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6c82a-ea16-5ff3-8bdf-84c0339a862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459994} :answer-field/id #uuid "4819ddf4-8130-5b59-a61d-9183708e79f6" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c9400fe-5e9b-5eeb-8918-63a684f4e2ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459995} {:answer/id #uuid "000331dd-d687-50e7-840d-4298a5368dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9400fe-5e9b-5eeb-8918-63a684f4e2ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459995} :answer-field/id #uuid "234e20cd-9790-5bf2-8ab0-5d985b7db758" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a258fde-3dcf-564c-9b6b-f6a8c2ff2d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459997} {:answer/id #uuid "708f2b4d-d226-5732-a090-fd16b632ea2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a258fde-3dcf-564c-9b6b-f6a8c2ff2d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459997} :answer-field/id #uuid "12022d23-fdca-5fdc-a369-46e825b1e2e8" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60c27a10-b6b0-5a54-9d51-0c91bf9fbc6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42591" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $P$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrices $Q$ and $S$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ is an elementary matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048920 :topic/id #uuid "cc887b1d-8841-507d-a99b-b7888c08a675" :topic/math-academy-id 1728 :topic/title "Finding the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Using Row Operations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} {:answer/id #uuid "7586863f-229d-578d-ac84-f0e761139eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec46523-5df6-5a30-a264-03c885caa2bd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed431171-2bbf-5c8c-afad-a46ecfc1b548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460007} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90e3cb2-cf8d-5f7e-8a1d-7e3fced79e84" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} {:answer/id #uuid "b44c80de-5afb-5ae0-9c0e-9042718b52cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b060f26-347b-584a-9045-d8d27b9e7501" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90c835e0-83aa-519b-9995-715569dd5d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-43000" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0303bd06-294e-5f7a-bbd2-b12abdeb93c5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 3x3 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048897 :topic/id #uuid "ca2d5c2b-c710-5912-bab0-623e5d6f5c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1731 :topic/title "Elementary 3x3 Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c4c87f-09c7-5e9a-b6a5-029734245381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477325} {:answer/id #uuid "44f62344-515d-5274-9c6e-607d5a5b1e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c4c87f-09c7-5e9a-b6a5-029734245381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477325} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18ab024-61b0-55dd-8cd5-3b5d03d5bd7f" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477632} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79ebd9f8-93bd-5df1-9313-eab2b5635228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477327} {:answer/id #uuid "379250a1-a18a-5cea-80a6-b6640f3f7561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "379250a1-a18a-5cea-80a6-b6640f3f7561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477328} :answer-field/id #uuid "645a4e8e-b0ab-5b4d-afb5-d13f5affc3a7" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477633} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93929904-e248-512d-967a-b6030ad20a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477329} {:answer/id #uuid "571eddfb-765e-505f-8b07-eee9c08d2c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "571eddfb-765e-505f-8b07-eee9c08d2c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477330} :answer-field/id #uuid "771dc8c0-f925-55a9-9eea-e2734e1718f4" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb7edba7-7f03-5a91-ad50-58a8e20f5eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-43509" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an elementary matrix is obtained by performing exactly one elementary row operation on the identity matrix $I.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $P$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from $I$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $Q$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=7{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=7{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $S$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =S\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ and $S$ are elementary matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae32fd46-e32d-5264-be56-b9a6b9f79deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448678} {:answer/id #uuid "26a1facd-428e-55da-ac4c-32b541a82e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae32fd46-e32d-5264-be56-b9a6b9f79deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448678} :answer-field/id #uuid "eafd7efd-50a5-5cc7-a3f7-e5846d88879f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ab8d57d-ec4f-5dec-889e-143e9572b107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448680} {:answer/id #uuid "47bc75b7-5946-50f4-aff7-ea09a3705121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ab8d57d-ec4f-5dec-889e-143e9572b107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448680} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7820977-9ada-53d1-a0cb-bfdd1f75154d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d435aca-2ad6-5e73-8567-2294af79b061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448682} {:answer/id #uuid "a0aae356-7958-595d-b625-5bacfd114390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0aae356-7958-595d-b625-5bacfd114390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448683} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3da2828-250e-5af8-b521-e5bccd76acc4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "995f3b18-ad68-56fb-a94d-9e7f0a50f6c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-47367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 2, & x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It is **not** continuous at $x=1$ but it is differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **III.** It is **not** differentiable on the interval $x\\in (-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement individually.\n\n- Statement I is false. First, we investigate the continuity of $f(x)$ . It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, $x=1.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}{x}^{2}={1}^{2}=1 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}{x}^{2}={1}^{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=2,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ (it is a removable discontinuity).\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1,$ it is also not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval that includes this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable in $x\\in (-2,2).$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78d7a514-ecfa-55cb-87c6-b60de1c022f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448708} {:answer/id #uuid "dc689acd-0734-5dcf-80c8-9704924c5f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc689acd-0734-5dcf-80c8-9704924c5f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448709} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5b60060-524b-5cf4-87fe-091fb1042d78" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eb89f53-77c8-596d-ae53-cd6a097dbbf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448710} {:answer/id #uuid "9e7743f7-78bf-58ff-9155-635e6f903288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eb89f53-77c8-596d-ae53-cd6a097dbbf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448710} :answer-field/id #uuid "13793ac0-8ac1-549e-a713-98a29ed44f94" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a43a32d-e760-5c98-a4e4-877d467394b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448712} {:answer/id #uuid "0a70e804-1854-50d9-892f-b441bea742d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a43a32d-e760-5c98-a4e4-877d467394b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448712} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8b7059-0041-56e3-a03b-3f0d2038120d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07b54935-f6c1-5cc5-a220-23bab58f39a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-47653" :question/problem "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n\n- **II.** $Ax=0$ has no solutions\n\n- **III.** The lines $6x+2y=1$ and $-3x+ky=-2$ intersect at infinitely many points" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n1\\. $A$ is invertible.\n\n2\\. The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n3\\. The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n4\\. The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n5\\. $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =6\\cdot k-2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6k+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $6k+6\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -1.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, there must be a unique zero solution to $Ax=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the lines must intersect at exactly one point.\n\nFinally, only statement I is true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 5" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481569} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481748}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80449399-3ae4-593f-8c3b-00bcdcc99727" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Outside of the Range of Cosecant" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048533 :topic/id #uuid "a7996653-9e76-59d9-b493-05cb731632cb" :topic/math-academy-id 1566 :topic/title "Elementary Trigonometric Equations Containing Cosecant"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45ba7a28-f5ab-5e8c-bc17-9d5aab25046f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460143} {:answer/id #uuid "80ce1dbd-10cc-59b6-9289-c909a77cba1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45ba7a28-f5ab-5e8c-bc17-9d5aab25046f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460143} :answer-field/id #uuid "d18cd2ef-70a9-5c85-8f02-b40a6d26a24e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460938} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "961c26f2-63c3-54fc-aeb9-e7648a950edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460145} {:answer/id #uuid "37d442a2-2f8a-5312-9b90-48b084ae5212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "961c26f2-63c3-54fc-aeb9-e7648a950edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460145} :answer-field/id #uuid "47f22d72-b197-553d-a5c2-7e8ef4b264d6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c87dfb-77a1-52ef-b8e7-8c3e4e543d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460147} {:answer/id #uuid "df82fb8f-576e-57ac-a09c-ca798d97ff40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df82fb8f-576e-57ac-a09c-ca798d97ff40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460148} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6bcfd7d-9311-5cec-a044-975a0cf459e8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c319e35c-f6f5-5224-8a19-cffd75e260ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-66002" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n- **I.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3$\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1$\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68350e0d-84ca-5b50-b05a-1bca3ceea40f" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 3x3 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049684 :topic/id #uuid "0aa448d3-ff23-589f-85d0-370c4ca9baa8" :topic/math-academy-id 1732 :topic/title "Finding the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using Row Operations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38974865-c7f9-5ffe-94d5-91b4e04ff444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460203} {:answer/id #uuid "c331e806-f9c0-5251-9556-a1753a1a204a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38974865-c7f9-5ffe-94d5-91b4e04ff444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460203} :answer-field/id #uuid "b09480df-6302-5589-833b-bf1d13779ebe" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "737acf5f-5cf1-5011-a7e5-0023a1a48528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460205} {:answer/id #uuid "6a401068-ebc7-5c00-9082-012e97f6e1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a401068-ebc7-5c00-9082-012e97f6e1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460206} :answer-field/id #uuid "263429d0-3ddb-5c95-8edf-09fb879b803a" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4512e449-e6ed-52cc-b346-7238689f5f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460207} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4a0baf-e0b9-5748-8c91-d7dd4ff84c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4512e449-e6ed-52cc-b346-7238689f5f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460207} :answer-field/id #uuid "154db06d-99a7-548d-9b02-b144426bc535" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf16f494-c482-58f3-9d08-1de06dd3fe97" :question/math-academy-id "q-78426" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19c33c51-bf11-5a81-a0fd-8381d8e0b9d7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Line Is a Subspace of Two-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051046 :topic/id #uuid "7cf616eb-2b54-52d2-8407-1b2fc912b2d9" :topic/math-academy-id 1853 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90bf2615-f44c-5a92-b7f7-16b4105c8c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477151} {:answer/id #uuid "ca27e4e3-8bca-5871-9395-a6380f99cd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca27e4e3-8bca-5871-9395-a6380f99cd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477152} :answer-field/id #uuid "27cef8a9-5b30-53f7-9387-8d249e05a639" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477545} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aca2503-832b-575e-b56c-b125e1b5c5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477153} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f4c934-20cf-5792-9fd6-4e318ffcf52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f4c934-20cf-5792-9fd6-4e318ffcf52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477154} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9674e23-7a9d-5e22-aede-cfbab89607f8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bfe5c36-5e7c-5bd5-87a1-4069378067df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477155} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f2d338-3f3e-5490-a9bc-b39400a94b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9f2d338-3f3e-5490-a9bc-b39400a94b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477156} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd7028b-5925-58dd-9e69-36d0f34bb338" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dad4bcf4-7bb7-58ca-92ea-68aab62ad28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477157} {:answer/id #uuid "a05fa06f-95fd-5a6f-8b50-f72c429bbdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a05fa06f-95fd-5a6f-8b50-f72c429bbdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477158} :answer-field/id #uuid "2211ec51-ee76-5442-bf6d-ce7726af963f" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44d1d34b-4b40-5331-8b03-073462e9a684" :question/math-academy-id "q-155956" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $x=2y$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- **II.** $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- **III.** $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **IV.** $L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $x=2y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2y \\\\ (0) & =2(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2a+2b \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2(a+b) \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $x=2y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2ka \\\\ ka\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $x=2y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83796fe8-f045-5dbc-94d1-6d6e031f3ed8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Line Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051046 :topic/id #uuid "7cf616eb-2b54-52d2-8407-1b2fc912b2d9" :topic/math-academy-id 1853 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24252954-787b-5287-ada3-c3c084627cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459561} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea7f730-2ff2-5228-b790-8f8914e58843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24252954-787b-5287-ada3-c3c084627cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459561} :answer-field/id #uuid "558fdbad-eec9-50d1-9396-20fe7193cb95" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f04425c-7df1-58ad-b1e6-f2932fcc8dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459563} {:answer/id #uuid "dacc05fc-1ec1-5c2a-8d1d-3483419a8522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f04425c-7df1-58ad-b1e6-f2932fcc8dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459563} :answer-field/id #uuid "8497150c-19f4-5c2a-ae83-13740f506308" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22251dfe-d083-5dc0-aef6-975964d95330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459565} {:answer/id #uuid "148689b1-11a7-55ba-b407-5c7f94bd335b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22251dfe-d083-5dc0-aef6-975964d95330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459565} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f6846b-3415-5ec5-80cb-0595a3ec6235" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0514bb18-c8aa-5a5a-a02c-b2ade3e4b60b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459567} {:answer/id #uuid "079aa3e4-f3eb-5f67-9f8d-9697c3429fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "079aa3e4-f3eb-5f67-9f8d-9697c3429fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459568} :answer-field/id #uuid "f181aeb8-c359-5992-b7c4-2c5057fd3737" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b679935-b7fe-5b87-9b05-95735d1a350e" :question/math-academy-id "q-155957" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in ${R}^{3}$ that passes through the points $(-2,2,-2)$ and $(3,-4,2).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $L$ contains the zero-vector\n\n- **II.** $L$ is closed under vector addition\n\n- **III.** $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **IV.** $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The direction vector of the line $L$ is \n\n$$\nd=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{5}=\\frac{y-2}{-6}=\\frac{z+2}{4}.\n$$\n\nBut this line does not pass through the origin since \n\n$$\n\\frac{(0)+2}{5}\\ne \\frac{(0)-2}{-6}\\ne \\frac{(0)+2}{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let's consider the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L$ (the position vectors of the given points). Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the point $(1,-2,0)$ does not belong to $L$ since\n\n$$\n\\frac{(1)+2}{5}\\ne \\frac{(-2)-2}{-6}\\ne \\frac{(0)+2}{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a750e3-d153-524f-a54e-d722127369f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448404} {:answer/id #uuid "474d3371-8932-5041-9ec0-7a2713e5c329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a750e3-d153-524f-a54e-d722127369f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448404} :answer-field/id #uuid "6751ef52-bd73-517e-81c4-c56485295df6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c6a2d4a-341d-5cb7-9f08-a6c31b8bf13a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448406} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f1e515-ad10-5a3e-8ac9-3eaf8f191a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3f1e515-ad10-5a3e-8ac9-3eaf8f191a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448407} :answer-field/id #uuid "4776a07a-b85f-5a19-a13c-2087f8f5df16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af0094a7-d9e0-57fc-84a4-bfce73870162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448408} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad95581-5f03-5403-ae4d-5a62d3cbd6d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ad95581-5f03-5403-ae4d-5a62d3cbd6d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448409} :answer-field/id #uuid "b99b2aa8-b962-5194-be9e-f3d0a51b7833" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ec28c6e-377f-591a-9037-3511702a70c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-155965" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$\n\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- **III.** The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+{a}_{3} & =2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-3+1 \\\\ -2-0+2 \\\\ 4-0+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b24b9fb-3a78-5b39-97db-5d260de94782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448410} {:answer/id #uuid "f64cc72e-31d2-5bec-9c8f-199c1ae77a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b24b9fb-3a78-5b39-97db-5d260de94782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448410} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc2eb58e-ea01-5c50-b62f-9127356e961b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a16cea7-d0c4-5953-9641-00bd84983fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448412} {:answer/id #uuid "3fafa4a0-feb2-53eb-9c91-01bf033b7cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fafa4a0-feb2-53eb-9c91-01bf033b7cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448413} :answer-field/id #uuid "90edb75f-056d-51fe-b4d6-0959b7052573" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1abdbc03-a454-57f6-bb48-be031db06b2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448414} {:answer/id #uuid "20dc8704-4e53-5add-b192-596188f94535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20dc8704-4e53-5add-b192-596188f94535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448415} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee14665-3f3f-5d5c-bf70-8e4c97353be2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62e09db0-cf5e-5972-a5d2-6baa771c45b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-155967" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- **III.** The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88045f96-4e5c-56f2-aa3d-094165238e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448416} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9e3a90-b6f1-5944-9c06-c0858870b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a9e3a90-b6f1-5944-9c06-c0858870b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448417} :answer-field/id #uuid "592d5ef9-838c-58f7-b2e0-f8df0b00d16c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76822f72-cfc5-5fec-9c40-af21257c06e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448418} {:answer/id #uuid "86511923-dda7-5828-95f9-4fb71d5328f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76822f72-cfc5-5fec-9c40-af21257c06e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448418} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ecd9ca-5548-5f7e-8c99-34f1ae5972c9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449249} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a519d51a-908f-5104-a290-489f7afd4cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448420} {:answer/id #uuid "42d3bc50-a4f9-59df-8456-d050d0382bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a519d51a-908f-5104-a290-489f7afd4cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448420} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ef3520a-4900-5830-be1a-16e5f59bc604" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d522f4eb-6fdb-5796-8d35-98401ee7b35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-156591" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+1-2 \\\\ 2+0-2 \\\\ 0+2-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19c33c51-bf11-5a81-a0fd-8381d8e0b9d7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Line Is a Subspace of Two-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051046 :topic/id #uuid "7cf616eb-2b54-52d2-8407-1b2fc912b2d9" :topic/math-academy-id 1853 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4aa7af-8e65-56ef-819b-139ea1e8f1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448422} {:answer/id #uuid "2065cab8-cb21-54d6-94e1-b4b41f0a9f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e4aa7af-8e65-56ef-819b-139ea1e8f1e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448422} :answer-field/id #uuid "10b6ea84-6376-54ab-96c2-52e2850b8611" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4c529a-16f2-5ba1-a671-c872c0a87c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448424} {:answer/id #uuid "5136518b-8276-5038-9702-9cadb0a02eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4c529a-16f2-5ba1-a671-c872c0a87c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448424} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f2baf9-c041-5c30-bc69-006f9e288c0d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b720d1d-4786-52f6-b181-142bfc0915cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448426} {:answer/id #uuid "976d669d-a25a-5e0d-8370-ea5f89cf2984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b720d1d-4786-52f6-b181-142bfc0915cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448426} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9656039-a18e-523c-a419-cc089ff54e48" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73990243-f849-5436-9398-edc0b840c742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448428} {:answer/id #uuid "806954d4-5596-58d9-a021-a4e661ee44cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "806954d4-5596-58d9-a021-a4e661ee44cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448429} :answer-field/id #uuid "4482a4af-af62-5f1a-a13f-0a50c8a9c069" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d2b6331-122d-5166-a305-241f7f5b32d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-156607" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $y=1-2x$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $L$ contains the zero-vector\n\n- **II.** $L$ is closed under vector addition\n\n- **III.** $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **IV.** $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 1-2x\\end{bmatrix},\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The coordinates of the zero-vector do not satisfy the equation $y=1-2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-2x \\\\ (0) & =1-2(0) \\\\ 0 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ from $L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0+1 \\\\ 1-1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHowever, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\notin L$ since substituting the coordinates into the equation, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-2x \\\\ (0) & =1-2(1) \\\\ 0 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $0\\notin L,$ this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since statements II and III are false, $L$ is *not* a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83796fe8-f045-5dbc-94d1-6d6e031f3ed8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Line Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051046 :topic/id #uuid "7cf616eb-2b54-52d2-8407-1b2fc912b2d9" :topic/math-academy-id 1853 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ac7fa6-59a2-56c7-9df0-60e6f9d373a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448430} {:answer/id #uuid "05d3173c-d6b0-53b5-b89c-0ce5e9739205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d3173c-d6b0-53b5-b89c-0ce5e9739205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448431} :answer-field/id #uuid "536d01eb-316b-5f78-85cc-6db641672f4e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca54fc57-c37e-51a6-a86f-a516fb08af34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448432} {:answer/id #uuid "dfdcb3c8-29fb-582c-af97-98c3b894e5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfdcb3c8-29fb-582c-af97-98c3b894e5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448433} :answer-field/id #uuid "e10c661f-1bbc-5bcf-8d4f-c1cfe52baa32" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1438a80e-a496-5dd2-92bf-5b533c7b0cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448434} {:answer/id #uuid "fa25c559-a416-5989-a7de-2ccfe3aaa0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa25c559-a416-5989-a7de-2ccfe3aaa0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448435} :answer-field/id #uuid "42431b57-7a25-535b-b215-21a57dd08e92" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bdae2ec-697d-519c-aca1-c162479973d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448436} {:answer/id #uuid "741b5375-4601-52f5-8731-edbe3e16c480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bdae2ec-697d-519c-aca1-c162479973d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448436} :answer-field/id #uuid "349d2e5e-d6cf-5d91-adb1-200683782dcc" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe544997-b5f0-5f74-9a6d-c604c1790f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-156679" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line in ${R}^{3}$ that passes through the points $(0,0,0)$ and $(1,-1,1).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $L$ contains the zero-vector\n\n- **II.** $L$ is closed under vector addition\n\n- **III.** $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **IV.** $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nFirst, note that the direction vector of the line $L$ is \n\n$$\nd=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in R,$ and the corresponding Cartesian equation is \n\n$$\nx=-y=z.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, from the definition of $L$ we have that the point $(0,0,0)$ is in $L.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ -b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ -b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ -a+(-b) \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a+b \\\\ -(a+b) \\\\ a+b\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the conditions $x=-y=z.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -a \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ k(-a) \\\\ ka\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}ka \\\\ -(ka) \\\\ ka\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the conditions $x=-y=z.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3018fd-9d16-578f-b050-966890844c9b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Plane Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051046 :topic/id #uuid "7cf616eb-2b54-52d2-8407-1b2fc912b2d9" :topic/math-academy-id 1853 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d72575