db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "750e5596-8cc4-5cb0-bba0-0744d296137c" :answer-field/key "Column 5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfb0514f-33ea-5674-8071-994ec564a12b" :question/math-academy-id "q-35391" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $4$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, $4$th, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"} :activity/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572820} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573333}] :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574063 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124880} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 12.324000000000002 :task-item/id #uuid "0702bd69-b0e8-4ac8-99a2-124d4584ff48" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574064} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "b787c6f6-5351-5e11-97e1-60d594c3bcbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921