4}=3{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+5{v}_{3},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$\n- **III.** ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, solving equation ${v}_{4}=3{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}{v}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{v}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${v}_{4}=3{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}+5{v}_{3},$ we have that\n\n$$\n3\\cdot {v}_{1}-2\\cdot {v}_{2}+5\\cdot {v}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {v}_{4}=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution, the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set by definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9ab99e2-da39-53de-8dfb-e2e72019e10c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574369} {:answer/id #uuid "f30354b0-6